    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43508" root="&#xA;                        مثل&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِثَالٌ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>Quality, made, manner, fashion,</i> and
<i>form;</i> (Msb;) <i>a model according to which another
thing is made or proportioned; a pattern,</i>
(<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِقْدَارٌ</span>) <i>by which a thing is measured, proportioned, or cut out:</i> (T:) <i>an example</i> of a class

of words, of a rule, &amp;c. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنْ غَيْرِ سَبْقِ مِثاَلٍ</span>
[<i>Without there having been any precedent</i>]. (Msb
in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قرح</span>, &amp;c.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [<i>A bed:</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَناَتُ المِثَالِ</span>
                        <i>The
daughters of the bed;</i> meaning <i>women.</i> (T in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بنى</span>.)

